# reduce-sum.xtl hand-lowered: '+ r_/ v of eight 16-bit numbers (the
# schedule makes it a tree of seven adders), one that wraps, and the
# largest item (a tree of comparators). The evaluator's own 64-bit
# sums (lines 1 and 3) are not circuit outputs.
# baseline: demo-reduce-sum 2,4,5
%v = input i16[8] 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8
%big = input i16[8] 10000 10000 10000 10000 10000 10000 10000 10000
%s = reduce add %v
%sb = reduce add %big
%l = reduce max %v
output %s %sb %l
